MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

the horseshoe prior is proper but is parameterized in a certain (efficient and stable) way in brms that cannot be captured by the function that allows to sample from priors. accordingly you currently cannot test point hypothesis using this approach, but you can use the bayes_factor function to compare the two models (one with and one without the restriction).

