I know you can add se(standard_error, sigma = TRUE)

But then, is this

normal_lpdf(Y[n] | mu[n], sqrt(sigma^2 + se2[n]))

supposed to be the same as the 8 schools model?

which roughly, without the non-centered parametrization should look like this:
target += normal_lpdf(theta[n] | mu[n],sigma)
target += normal_lpdf(Y[n] | theta[n],se[n])

And another question that I have is if there is any reference to the type of parametrization that brms is using with sigma=TRUE.

Thanks!
Bruno

