m <- brm(effect_size | se(standard_error) ~ 1 + (1 | study), data = d)

and

m <- brm(effect_size | se(standard_error, sigma = TRUE) ~ 1, data = d)

lead to the same estimates of the intercept, but you don't get esimates for theta in the latter model, since they are implicitely handled as residuals.

I suggest you try out both models on the 8 schools example.

