> > Your fit_brms is not correct. It should be
> >
> > fit_brms<- brm(y | se(sigma) ~ 0 + intercept + (1|school), ...)
> >
> > where school is an identifier of the observations in your data set:
> >
> > dat$school <- 1:nrow(dat)
> >
> > Then, sd(Intercept), which you will see in the summary output, will take over the role of sigma.
> >
> >

> > 2018-02-12 18:02 GMT+01:00 Bruno Nicenboim <bruno.n...@gmail.com>:

> > > Sorry to bother with the same, but I still don't get it, there's no sigma in the first brms model (fit_brms)!
